{"exteraless":{"description":"exteraless is a fork of NagramX that implements exteraGram's features open-source.\n\nThe special focus is plugin security. In exteraGram a plugin is not restricted in any way; here it comes with a permission model and isolation: a plugin declares what it needs, you see that on the install sheet, and it gets only what was declared.","screenshots":["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Azt36/Orion-Store-assets-repo/refs/heads/main/exteraless/Screenshot_2026-09-13-22-41-30-31_57d100c9485356736d8e3fe7d156f6f2.jpg","https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Azt36/Orion-Store-assets-repo/refs/heads/main/exteraless/Screenshot_2026-09-13-22-41-40-88_57d100c9485356736d8e3fe7d156f6f2.jpg","https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Azt36/Orion-Store-assets-repo/refs/heads/main/exteraless/Screenshot_2026-09-13-22-41-44-67_57d100c9485356736d8e3fe7d156f6f2.jpg","https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Azt36/Orion-Store-assets-repo/refs/heads/main/exteraless/Screenshot_2026-09-13-22-41-47-96_57d100c9485356736d8e3fe7d156f6f2.jpg","https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Azt36/Orion-Store-assets-repo/refs/heads/main/exteraless/Screenshot_2026-09-13-22-41-57-29_57d100c9485356736d8e3fe7d156f6f2.jpg"]}}